-- title:
--   Order of a principal divisor above a supersingular node
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a nonzero $N$ with $q\nmid N$, an algebraically closed perfect field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $red\colon A\to k$, modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr`, integrality hypotheses $h\alpha,h\beta$ for the two level-raising maps from level $N$ to level $Nq$, a place specialisation $P$ for these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$ which is a model (the two divisor laws and the two cusp laws), satisfies the order law at Frobenius-fixed affine places, and satisfies the regularity law and the node value law for a finite set $W_0$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` all of which are rational, affine and have supersingular $j$-invariant. Let $K\le K'$ be intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with $K'/\mathbb Q$ finite, and let $w\in W_0$ be such that its translate $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\,q\,k\,N\cdot w$ also lies in $W_0$, such that the value integrality law holds at $w$, and such that $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K\,w\le R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K'\,w$ (these rings consist of the functions of level $Nq$ integral for $R_1$, for $R_2$ and for every place $V$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V=w$, whose expansions lie in the subfield generated by the constants of $K$, resp. $K'$, together with $j$ and $j_{Nq}$). Assume further: an element $\varpi$ of the coefficient ring $A\cap K'$ whose multiples are exactly the elements killed by $red$, an exponent $e_K\ge 1$ and a unit $\varepsilon$ with $q=\varpi^{e_K}\varepsilon$; node coordinates $c=(x,y)$ over $K$ at $w$ (so the first residue of $x$ vanishes, the second residue of $x$ has order $1$ at the Frobenius translate of $w$, the second residue of $y$ vanishes, and the first residue of $y$ has order $1$ at $w$), an exponent $e_w\ge 1$ and a unit $u$ of the larger node ring with $xy=(R.\mathrm{nodeConst}\,K'\,w\,\varpi)^{e_we_K}u$; that the ideal generated by the constant $\varpi$ and the images of $x,y$ in $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K'\,w$ is maximal, is the only maximal ideal, and is the maximal ideal of that local Noetherian ring; that the ideals generated by $\varpi$ with $x$, resp. with $y$, are prime, with $y$ outside the first and $x$ outside the second; and that every element of the node ring differs from some constant by a non-unit. Finally let $f\ne 0$ be a function of level $Nq$ whose expansion lies in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N*q) K'`, assume every element of that field is a quotient of two elements of $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K'\,w$ with nonzero denominator, and let $c_1,c_2\in K'$ be nonzero with $c_1f$ in the integers of $R.R_1$ and $c_2f$ in those of $R.R_2$, both with nonzero residue. Then for the divisor $D$ given by $D(V)=\operatorname{ord}_V f$ one has $$\sum_{V\in\operatorname{supp}D,\ P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V=w} D(V)\ \le\ \operatorname{ord}_w\big(R.\mathrm{residue}_1(c_1f)\big)+\operatorname{ord}_{\mathrm{arithFrobC}\,q\,k\,N\cdot w}\big(R.\mathrm{residue}_2(c_2f)\big).$$
--
--   This is the local contribution of a supersingular node to the specialisation of a principal divisor: the total order of $f$ at the places of the level-$Nq$ curve lying over the node $w$ is bounded by the sum of the orders of the two normalised residues of $f$ along the two branches, at $w$ and at its arithmetic Frobenius translate. Whereas the order law at Frobenius-fixed affine places asserts an equality for such places, here only an upper bound is asserted, and no condition of being Frobenius-fixed is imposed; it is used in the two forms of `depthDual_add_mem_range_gramMap_of_isPrincipal`.
